   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 381 of the laws of 2010 amending the tax law relating\nto the imposition of an occupancy tax in the village of Rye Brook, in relation\nto extending the expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S6721",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6721-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 381 of 2010",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6721\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 381 of the laws of 2010 amending the tax law\nrelating to the imposition of an occupancy tax in the village of Rye\nBrook, in relation to extending the expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nTo extend the authority of the village of Rye Brook to impose a room\noccupancy tax not to exceed 3W.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 extends the authority of the village of Rye Brook to impose a\nroom occupancy tax until September 1, 2027.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill extends the current village of Rye Brook occupancy tax. The\nvillage of Rye Brook has used these non-property tax revenues to offset\ncapital expenditures.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022: S7683/A8666, L 2022 ch 405\n\n2019: S5083/A6554, L 2019 ch 211\n\n2016: S6079/A9072, L 2016 ch 290\n\n2013: S2594/A3823, L 2013 ch 108\n\n2010: S1180A/A231A, L 2010 ch 381\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
